    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d946">

                <pb facs="0836" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72115/2738b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Belgium</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitlock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-29T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1916, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>243. Please report by cable situation regarding Belgian deportations, whether the
                    deportations are continuing, and if not, what <pb facs="0837" n="665"
                        xml:id="pg665"/> percentage of those who have been deported are being
                    returned to Belgium. Interest in this whole subject is increasing in the United
                    States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
